drylab-onlyoffice: a modified version of ONLYOFFICE Docs Community
==================================================================

This repository builds a MODIFIED VERSION of ONLYOFFICE Docs (Document
Server) Community Edition 10.0.0.1, the original software developed by
Ascensio System SIA (https://www.onlyoffice.com). It is based on the
upstream image onlyoffice/documentserver:10.0.0.1 and on the upstream
source at https://github.com/ONLYOFFICE/DocumentServer (tag v10.0.0.1).

ONLYOFFICE is a trademark of Ascensio System SIA. This build is not an
official ONLYOFFICE product and is not endorsed by Ascensio System SIA. We
refer to it only as "based on ONLYOFFICE Docs".

Modified by: Drylab (GitHub organisation Drylab-AI)
Date(s) of modification: 2026-11-23 (theme, image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.1);
2026-11-23 (layout v2, image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.2); 2026-11-24 (polish,
image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.3); 2026-11-24 (notice line, image tag
10.0.0.1-drylab.4); 2026-11-24 (spreadsheet and presentation look, image
tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.5; includes one spreadsheet save fix); 2026-11-24
(About button, image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.6)

What was modified (web-apps, plus two colour constants in sdkjs since
drylab.5 and one About button since drylab.6; server and binaries are
unchanged)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Added web-apps/apps/common/main/resources/drylab/drylab.css (source:
   drylab-theme/drylab.css). A CSS theme for the light "White" interface
   theme: white header row, tabs styled as plain text menu items, the
   toolbar as one rounded light pill, a soft grey canvas around the page, a
   slimmer status bar, a smaller and muted (still visible) ONLYOFFICE logo,
   and Drylab's green as the accent colour. It also adds a line to the
   About panel stating that this is a modified version, by whom and when,
   that it is based on ONLYOFFICE Docs by Ascensio System SIA, the licence,
   and where the modified source is.

2. Edited web-apps/apps/{documenteditor,spreadsheeteditor,presentationeditor}
   /main/index.html: one <link> to drylab.css inserted before </head>, with
   an HTML comment stating the modification and its date (script:
   scripts/patch-index.sh, run in the Dockerfile).

3. Regenerated the precompressed (.gz) copies of the touched files when the
   image has them.

4. Layout v2 (2026-11-23, image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.2), same CSS file,
   still CSS only:
   - the menu row (tabs) is plain 14 px text starting at the x of the
     integrator's document title above the editor, with the ONLYOFFICE
     logo moved to the right end of that row (still visible, 70 px wide,
     60 % opacity, full on hover);
   - ONLYOFFICE's header user avatar, header search and header Share
     button are hidden (the integrator's bar has Share; search stays in
     the side strip and on Ctrl+F);
   - the toolbar is one 40 px rounded pill (radius 24 px) on a single row:
     ONLYOFFICE's two stacked button rows sit side by side, its tall
     buttons are icon-only (the same state ONLYOFFICE uses when a toolbar
     is narrow), and the paragraph style gallery shows only the current
     style plus its dropdown with every style. ONLYOFFICE's own overflow
     ("more") menu still takes whatever does not fit;
   - slimmer status bar (26 px) and a slightly stronger page border on the
     grey canvas.
   The About panel and its side-strip button are unchanged (in 10.0.0.1
   that button is the only way into the About panel).

5. Polish (2026-11-24, image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.3), same CSS file, still
   CSS only:
   - the toolbar row is fixed for tabs whose controls carry captions: the
     View tab's "Zoom" caption sits beside its field instead of wrapping
     below the pill, Layout's indent/spacing spinners and the
     presentation galleries (shapes, transitions, animations) fit the
     40 px pill, and two-line captions (Add Animation, Preview) become
     icon buttons with their tooltip. ONLYOFFICE's own overflow ("more")
     menu still collects what does not fit;
   - menu row items are 13 px (were 14 px);
   - hidden collaboration chrome the integrator does not use: the
     Collaboration tab (comments, track changes, compare and chat are off
     in the integrator's config), the users counter ("who is editing"),
     the Editing/Viewing mode switch and the header close button.
     Co-editing itself is unchanged. The Protection tab is removed by the
     integrator's config (document.permissions.protect: false), not by CSS;
   - ONLYOFFICE's About entry in the left strip is HIDDEN, at the request
     of the integrator. See "Where the legal notices are
     shown" below.

6. Spreadsheet and presentation look (2026-11-24, image tag
   10.0.0.1-drylab.5):
   - drylab.css (CSS): spreadsheet column letters and row numbers in a
     light grey with hairline borders and the selected header tinted
     green (ONLYOFFICE's own --canvas-cell-title-* theme variables); the
     formula bar as one white line under the toolbar (cell name, an "fx"
     label in place of the function icon, the formula input); flat,
     rounded sheet tabs with the active one tinted green; muted selection
     stats in the status bar; in presentations a white speaker-notes
     strip under the slide and a hairline beside the thumbnails;
   - sdkjs/cell/sdk-all.js: exactly two colour constants changed, the
     cell grid lines (rgb 202,202,202 -> 226,227,227) and the active-cell
     / selection outline (rgb 72,121,92 -> 0,157,81). A comment line at
     the top of the file states the modification and its date (script:
     scripts/patch-js.sh, run in the Dockerfile; the build fails if the
     constants are not found exactly once). Nothing else in sdkjs changes;
   - web-apps/apps/spreadsheeteditor/main/app/controller/Main.js: one event
     listener added. The public API call docEditor.blurFocus() now also
     closes the spreadsheet cell editor the way clicking another cell does,
     so a cell the user is still typing in is kept when the integrator
     saves from outside the editor. A comment line at the top of the file
     states the modification and its date (same script).

7. About button (2026-11-24, image tag 10.0.0.1-drylab.6):
   - web-apps/apps/{documenteditor,spreadsheeteditor,presentationeditor}/
     main/app/template/LeftMenu.template: one "About" button (ONLYOFFICE's
     own (i) icon and localized "About" hint) added to the left strip;
   - .../main/app/view/LeftMenu.js: the button's click calls the public
     Gateway's internalMessage('drylab:about'), which posts
     onInternalMessage {type: "drylab:about"} to the integrator page. It
     does not open ONLYOFFICE's About panel and sends no document data;
   - drylab.css: the button is pinned to the bottom of the strip, same
     size and colour as the strip's other buttons.
   Each changed file carries a "Modified by Drylab" line with the date
   (script: scripts/patch-about.sh, run in the Dockerfile; the build fails
   if an anchor is not found exactly once).

Where the legal notices are shown (since 10.0.0.1-drylab.6)
------------------------------------------------------------

With ONLYOFFICE's About entry hidden, every editor (document, spreadsheet,
presentation) has one "About" (i) button at the bottom of its left strip.
It opens the integrator's (Drylab's) About dialog, which reads
"Based on the open-source ONLYOFFICE Docs (AGPL v3)" and
"ONLYOFFICE is a trademark of Ascensio System SIA.", with one Close button. The dialog is translated
into English, Vietnamese, Japanese and Chinese; "ONLYOFFICE Docs" and
"AGPL v3" are never translated.

History: until drylab.3 the integrator showed a longer notice in an
"About this editor" (i) dialog in its header; from drylab.4 to drylab.5
one muted line in its header bar, "Based on the open-source ONLYOFFICE
Docs (AGPL v3)" (trademark sentence as tooltip). That line was moved into
this button by the integrator.

